VALUES (588, '1', $t$ASK 588: the judges' question round is live on every fresh run, with one continuation pass (D7, ruling 515)$t$,
  $t$Before they judge, the judges put their questions to the debaters, and the debaters answer, on every fresh live run, as the operator asked under rulings 413 and 414. Every judge who decides the run reads the same questions and answers, and keeps reading them in every later turn. A fault in the question round never stops a run: it is recorded and the run goes on without the round. (plan rev 0, section 1.) With it, by the operator's rulings 514 and 515: a judge may ask a continuation of another judge's question and still keeps its own question (D7).$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 in two writes on the operator's two presses at 00:25 CST 2026-11-24 in W4's thread, cards "Write ASK 588" and "Write after 588" (D7), with no run live (last execution 42071) (Wall 11399; audit 41213). Write 1, ASK 588: engine moMxiV4Irg1uRBZN 7536d7bf to f9e06f5e-d557-494e-a495-65d38898bf04, 398 to 407 nodes (9 new: QR Answer D Build, D Route, D anthropic, D Done, C Build, C Route, C anthropic, C openrouter, C Done; 35 changed); child MqQHRl7mQQ0z8QdT a7113b8d to 2d5bdc94-752e-4d6c-8415-adf89ecb8c2f (Shared Library only). Write 2, D7: engine f9e06f5e to 06ba53ad-2029-44cb-90fc-21ad420f4028, 420 nodes (13 QR Follow nodes new; Init Seats and QR Merge changed); the child is unchanged. What is live: the question round runs on every fresh run unless the body sends question_trial:false, and in a regrade only when question_trial:true is sent; the dry-only gate of Init Seats and the dry-only throw of QR Ask Build are removed. Each panel judge puts one question to each debater in a fixed form the program writes (MEANING, FIT, and AGREE for a closing contradiction; ruling 414 item 2); each question is checked (exact quotation from the round named, the term in the quotation, the verse named in it, no verse the debater has not cited; one return); each debater answers by its own model and route (Anthropic direct or OpenRouter); all six questions and answers stand in one block before the transcript in every judge body and every later turn (send-back, gate, late gate, cures 1 to 3, reserve, alternates in the engine and the child, panel check); a fault skips the round and the run goes on; NO RECORD IS STORED (W4's mistake, reported at Wall 11403; W1's grade at Wall 11393 missed it too, because its test T6.1 tested the node's text and not its place in the live path, as W1 states at Wall 11404): the card said the questions and answers are stored in review_notes on the line "[QUESTION ROUND v1: ...]", but on a live run Build Save Body runs before the round, so that line never writes; the judges do receive the questions and answers, and only the record is lost. The fix, ASK 588 R (two new nodes QR Record Build and QR Record, a new table odv1_question_round_log; commit e3e84ce4, target 28168cf1), was with W1 for grading and NOT written when this row was drafted; it is not in this row. D7: after the six answers each judge may put at most one continuation to each debater, only on a question ANOTHER judge put to that debater; it keeps its own question (Q1 to Q6 stay, continuations are Q7 and after); a continuation of the judge's own question is dropped and recorded (ruling 515); switch qr_follow, on with the round unless qr_follow:false is sent. The operator's choices of 00:01 CST 2026-11-24 in W4's thread, as Wall 11392 gives them: D1 "A now, B as its own ASK" (an answer explains and is never counted as a round); D3 "Keep it" (the AGREE form); "One continuation pass"; "Hold the run". W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11401): engine f9e06f5e equals target 024290a7 (407 nodes, 0 differences, connections equal); engine 06ba53ad equals target 7ede01fb (420 nodes, 0 differences); child 2d5bdc94 equals target 16ed1670 (156 nodes, 0 differences); t588 82 PASS and t588f 37 PASS on the live fetches; syn588f 378 parts, 0 errors. IN PART, because nothing of it has run: the new graph first executes live (n8n cannot run it offline), and the step after the write, a dry regrade of run 42071 with question_trial:true launched by the operator, had not been made when this row was drafted. The path of the grades: W4's read, PASS with B1 to B5 (Wall 11379, as plan588.md states); plan rev 0, PASS with F1 to F4 (Wall 11386); the 588 build, PASS (Wall 11393); the D7 build rev 0, FAIL on F1, since it let a judge continue its own question against ruling 515 (Wall 11395); D7 rev 1, PASS (Wall 11397). Stated limits (cards 588 and D7): the enforcer turn (Judge Enforcer Build) does not see the block; the single judge path is not connected (Build Independent Verdict has no parent); the answers are not counted as rounds (D1 B is its own ASK, not numbered in what W3 read); the round is skipped when a panel judge seat is not an OpenRouter seat or a debater's family is neither Anthropic nor OpenRouter; a continuation is not a contradiction candidate. Why it was not live before: ruling 413 approved the round "as a TRIAL ... run only on the dry re-grade of run 32404" and ruling 414 kept Commitment 8 "in the TRIAL posture only"; it ran in four dry regrades (34299, 34626, 34703, 34780) and no seat brought the card to make it live (Wall 11378; ruling row 512). RUN REVISION (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed or that a path is unexercised, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42373-tg0w4edj (debate_results e7f6922f, row created 17:21 CST 2026-11-24; engine 20db58ee, child 74353c40; anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 as the Oracle defending against anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; outcome UNDERDETERMINED, panel BROKEN 2-1). The round ran live by the Anthropic answer route and the judges read it. UNEXERCISED: the continuation pass (follow-up NONE for all six pairs) and the OpenRouter answer route. Where the block stood in each judge's request is in the execution only (W4's read is owed). The anchor fix that let the round run has its own row (ASK 588 rev F1). The first fresh run after the write, 42234, stored SKIPPED (log row 1), and run 42283 stored RAN (log row 2) and ended in error at the judges' call. In this run no panel send-back was sent (53 of 58 rows read "NOT SENT: no panel request for this seat"; the cause is the ASK 611 build, since fixed by fix 2 and not shown by a run), so nothing that needs a panel send-back was shown. The operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks two live runs with no issues; status stays 'read back'. RUN REVISION 42517 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed or that a path is unexercised, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42517-5yb0fmgv (debate_results fd0edbff, row saved 22:11 CST 2026-11-24; launch 21:50 CST; engine 2df7f6fa and child aad0ad9c by the write records; openai/gpt-6.2-sol as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; all eight rounds stored; THE PANEL FAILED at Panel Check on seat hydrogen and NO VERDICT exists; no judgment row and no enforcer row was written; cost 3.8227). The round ran live a second time: odv1_question_round_log id 4, status RAN, dry false. The OpenRouter answer route, unexercised in run 42373, carried the answers of both sides (call_costs "QR Answer" 3 for openai/gpt-6.2-sol and "QR Answer C openrouter" 3), and a follow-up was asked and answered ("QR Follow Ask" 3, "QR Follow C openrouter" 1), so the continuation pass ran for one pair at least. NOT SHOWN: the judges' use of the round (no judgment stored) and the Anthropic route in this run. This run is NOT a clean run: the panel failed and nothing after Panel Check ran (ASK 629), so it is not counted as one of the two live runs with no issues. The operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks two live runs with no issues; status stays 'read back'. RUN REVISION 42528 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed, that a path is unexercised, or what objective_met is, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42528-dqwbcshc (debate_results e0e528d8, row saved 22:59 CST 2026-11-24; launch 22:26 CST, ended with success 23:42 CST; engine 2df7f6fa and child aad0ad9c by the write records; google/gemini-4-hydrogen as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; every stage ran and no error row was written; outcome UNGRADED, panel 0-0 with 3 not counted under the debate rule; three judgments and 659 enforcer rows stored; cost 11.1907). The round ran live on a run that completed the judging: odv1_question_round_log id 5, status RAN, dry false; six questions (two each from qwen4max, sol and sol62), all six checks PASSED; three follow-up questions asked and PASSED. Both sides answered through OpenRouter, and the defender's follow-up answer went through "QR Follow D openrouter", a route no earlier run showed. The three judgments hold the word QUESTION (W3's search; how each judge used the round was not read). DEFECTS in this run: the defender's answer to question 3 was cut (finish length); sol62's follow-up quotes the question itself as the unanswered part. W3 counts this as the first of the two live runs with no issue that the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks, for the OpenRouter route (AAR graded PASS by W1, Wall 11941); objective_met stays 'in part' and status stays 'read back' until the second.$t$,
