  to_jsonb($t$23:36 CST 2026-11-23, W3 thread (ruling row 512): "Why in the hell would we build something and turn it off? ... That was a feature I requested ... it had nothing to do with a dry run." 23:45 CST (row 513): "A1.. I definitely want back." 23:47 CST (row 514): "A1 is designed to remove any gaps before the judges make their decision. If there's any ambiguity, if there's anything that was in between the lines, the judges get to ask each participant a question so that they can better make a more full decision." 23:51 CST (row 515): "no, there's no follow-up question. It's just that I was asked that, is it okay for a judge to ask a continuation question from the previous judge, but the judge still got to keep his original question ... Because the answer may not satisfy one of the other judges, so they can ask a continuation question from the question that came before them". His choices of 00:01 CST 2026-11-24 in W4's thread, as Wall 11392 gives them: D1 "A now, B as its own ASK"; D3 "Keep it"; "One continuation pass"; "Hold the run". His presses at 00:25 CST 2026-11-24 in W4's thread: "Write ASK 588" and "Write after 588" (audit 41213; W1 Wall 11401 item 1).$t$::text),
